    "result_text": "All 284 tests pass with no failures or errors.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `sharesHousehold` flag on owner creation. When a new owner is created, the field is set to `true` if another owner already has the same address and city, otherwise `false` \u2014 and creation is always allowed.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added the `sharesHousehold` boolean (read-only) property to the `Owner` response schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes it.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a persisted `sharesHousehold` field (`@Column(name = \"shares_household\")`) with getter/setter, following the existing pattern for `namesakeCount`/`membershipTier`. MapStruct maps it into the DTO automatically.\n\n3. **`src/main/java/.../rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 In `addOwner`, compute and set the flag before saving via a new `sharesHousehold(Owner)` helper that checks existing owners for a matching address and city (comparison normalized for case/whitespace, consistent with the other duplicate checks). Creation still proceeds regardless.\n\n4. **DB schemas** (`db/h2`, `db/hsqldb`, `db/mysql`, `db/postgres`) \u2014 Added the `shares_household` column so the value persists and is returned on subsequent `GET /api/owners/{id}`.\n\nThe new `Cp17Tests` (first owner at an address \u2192 `false`; second at the same address+city \u2192 `true`) passes, along with the full suite (284 tests, 0 failures).",
